virglrenderer: bind a GL program only when it changes

What: vrend_use_program() remembers, per sub context (one GL context each),
which program or pipeline is bound and skips the GL calls when the same one is
asked for again. Anything that may change bindings behind its back drops every
remembered binding: deleting a program or pipeline (names get reused), the GL
blitter, and binds from paths that do not know the current sub context
(transfers, read-back). OMACVM_VIRGL_PROGRAM_CACHE=0 binds on every draw again.
Why: vrend_draw_vbo calls vrend_use_program on every draw, so a WebGL page that
draws each object on its own (WebGL Aquarium: one draw per fish) binds the same
program hundreds of thousands of times a second. Apple's GL treats each
glUseProgram as a program change and rebuilds its draw state on the next draw:
measured on an M4, 0.39 us extra per draw (the draw rate drops 38 %).
Test: Tests/virgl/test-program-binds.c (colours after program switches, the
same program with new constants, a read-back, a destroyed shader, two sub
contexts; the cache really skips).

